From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 10:36:13 -1000
Subject: [PATCH 41/63] [cuttlefish][multi-device] Make vhost-device-vsock
 per-instance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
# Motivation:
Developers running multiple emulator types simultaneously on macOS (e.g. phone + watch) need each instance to manage its own vsock daemon. Previously, only the first instance started vhost_device_vsock with VM parameters for ALL instances, so stopping the first instance killed vsock connectivity for all others.

```
  BEFORE (shared daemon):             AFTER (per-instance daemons):

  run_cvd (instance 1)                run_cvd (instance 1)
       |                                   |
       v                                   v
  vhost_device_vsock ──> VM1,VM2      vhost_device_vsock ──> VM1
       |                              /tmp/vsock_3_501/
       X (stop instance 1)
       |                              run_cvd (instance 2)
  VM2 loses vsock!                         |
                                           v
                                      vhost_device_vsock ──> VM2
                                      /tmp/vsock_4_501/
```

# Overview:
Each run_cvd now starts its own vhost_device_vsock daemon with only its own VM configuration. Each instance uses unique socket paths (/tmp/vsock_{CID}_{UID}/), eliminating conflicts and enabling independent instance start/stop. Remove CuttlefishConfig dependency from VhostDeviceVsock (only needs InstanceSpecific).
